#40301
An Obsidian Passage~
   This grand hall is carved of solid obsidian.  The walls, ceiling and floor
are of this black smooth substance.  Light from several smoldering brands set
in iron sconces play and dance on the walls, where it is not covered by the
massive wall hangings and curtains that begin near the entrance to the west.  
The ceiling must be at least forty feet high, the width of the corridor doubly
that.  The entire hall dwarfs any visitors, save for those of similar
dimensions to its architects.    
~
